1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
A reservation system has to keep
its promises,

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,380
even when requests are repeated,

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,940
or a restaurant changes its plans.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:12,180
This is Tablekeeper, built by three agents
in BAND.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:16,720
Here is the accepted application with
fictitious demonstration data.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:19,900
We search for a table, select a time,

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:23,140
confirm a reservation and retrieve
its reference.

8
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,300
An unknown reference produces a
clear error.

9
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:29,840
Behind this workflow are four
complete stages

10
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:32,180
and an independently reviewed result.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,620
The Coordinator carries the full
assignment and its acceptance criteria.

12
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:42,280
The Builder owns the implementation.

13
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:47,660
The Verifier checks the exact revision
independently and can reject it.

14
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,800
Their standing mandates describe
these responsibilities

15
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:53,440
without encoding the reservation contract.

16
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,980
This is the original BAND room.

17
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,920
A numbered hand-off carries the cumulative
task with hashes

18
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,060
to check completeness.

19
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:04,980
These are real messages and results from
the selected run,

20
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:06,580
inspected after completion.

21
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,520
The most useful review was a rejection.

22
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,980
Public checks had passed, but the
Verifier found

23
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,360
that an imported, tampered closure plan
could later confirm

24
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:21,380
a reservation on a closing table.

25
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:23,520
The Builder repaired validation.

26
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:26,820
The independent re-check required the
invalid import

27
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:29,860
to return an error and leave the
destination unchanged.

28
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:32,240
It then approved the repaired commit.

29
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,440
The original record preserves the defect,
the correction,

30
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:38,840
and acceptance of revision 96AB4B8.

31
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:48,230
Stage 1 establishes atomic operations,

32
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:51,530
idempotent writes, and state export
and import.

33
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:55,990
Stage 2 adds the browser workflow and
recovery from stale state

34
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:57,230
and lost responses.

35
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,710
Stage 3 introduces policies

36
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:04,170
that take effect over time while keeping
accepted booking terms truthful.

37
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:08,090
Stage 4 adds series changes and
closure replanning

38
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:10,250
with preview and atomic application.

39
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:14,510
Each stage remains a complete service with
its own Dockerfile

40
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:15,630
and run instructions.

41
00:02:16,410 --> 00:02:18,870
The application itself needs no
model call.

42
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,480
The independent clean clone passed the
public checks

43
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,280
for all four stages in isolated mode.

44
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,880
The delivery ties these reports to the
accepted source,

45
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:34,180
three generic mandates, and the original
full BAND export.

46
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,520
The documentation records design choices,
elapsed time,

47
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,080
measured partial model usage, and
recovery history.

48
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:46,080
It distinguishes subscription usage from a
billed project cost.

49
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,380
Public checks support the result.

50
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,380
Private evaluation remains the
organizers' decision.

51
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:53,932
The evidence is available for inspection.

52
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:59,020
Recovery was needed between stages and
during Stage 4.

53
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,780
The operator restored runtime
files, infrastructure,

54
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:05,040
and the same agents and threads,

55
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:07,440
then sent one administrative notice.

56
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,780
There were no operator production edits or
repeated stage tasks.

57
00:03:12,039 --> 00:03:13,420
We disclose this intervention

58
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:16,000
and do not claim uninterrupted autonomy.

59
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,160
Tablekeeper brings together a
working service,

60
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,040
reproducible stages, and the
original record

61
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:24,200
of how the team built and checked it.

